HOW TO READ A PLANT (docs/queue-2026-11-06b.md rule 15)
  A plant is a fault I introduce. CAUGHT means at least one test turns red
  because of it, which is the good outcome. MISSED means everything stayed
  green, which is a finding.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. What A3.11 changed, and whether it makes the test stronger or weaker

  $ git show 45409e3 -- novacore/src/novacore/skills.py novacore/tests/test_skills.py

  skills.py, SlotDefinition.validate, TEXT branch:
    -            # Multi-line allowed, but control characters like NUL or shell backticks rejected
    -            if "\x00" in val_str or "`" in val_str:
    -                raise ValueError(f"slot '{self.name}' contains forbidden control characters")
    +            # Multi-line allowed, but control characters like NUL, shell backticks, or expansion syntax rejected
    +            if "\x00" in val_str or "`" in val_str or "$(" in val_str or "${" in val_str:
    +                raise ValueError(f"slot '{self.name}' contains forbidden control or expansion characters")

  test_skills.py gains exactly one test, test_text_slot_rejects_expansion_syntax,
  which asserts ValueError for "Notes with $(cat /etc/passwd)" and
  "Notes with ${EVIL}".

  Is the new test load-bearing? Plant S-P3 (section 5) reverts the two new
  conditions and the new test goes red, so yes. Is any existing test weakened?
  No: the diff adds conditions and adds a test, and removes nothing. Does it
  change behaviour for values that were already accepted? Yes, by design: a TEXT
  slot now refuses "$(" and "${" anywhere, including in a maths note that
  contains them harmlessly. That is a deliberate narrowing, not a bug, but it is
  a narrowing of what the owner can type into a notes field.
  Verdict on A3.11 for these files: stronger. The change is a real gate with a
  real test, unlike the shuttle.py half (see docs/reviews/e2-freebuff-r2.log
  section 8, where the new test pins a message and not the refusal).

